03
The judging matrix
Raw traffic answers "who is biggest," not "who should we learn from." Because you are building a hybrid decision tool for families, the matrix deliberately weights breadth of decisions covered and whether the site actually helps you decide and act as heavily as reach. Google reviews were dropped as a factor: content sites don't have them (they belong to movers with physical branches), so they would only measure the marketplace archetype.

20% Reach & authority — traffic, backlinks, domain age
20% Feature breadth — how many relocation decisions it covers
15% Data depth & freshness — coverage, structure, currency
15% Decision utility — tools & personalization vs static text
10% UX & polish
10% Trust & transparency — sourcing, methodology, reviews
10% Monetization proof — durable, demonstrated model
